qore (3.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Binary Module API 2.0: modules use QoreModuleInfo-based registration
  * Added required build dependencies: nghttp2, brotli, zstd, lz4
  * Updated module ABI to 2.0
  * Use quilt source format and declare complete, versioned build dependencies.
  * Require offline builds with packaged dependencies; retain upstream CMake
    FetchContent behavior for ordinary developer builds.
  * Complete compiler/tool file lists, build and install documentation, and split
    remote debugging tools with their YAML dependency.
  * Honor dpkg build flags, remove AOT build-directory RUNPATHs, and generate
    shared-library metadata with debhelper.
  * Add installed-package tests and document stable/LTS dependency backports.
  * Isolate build-time Qore module lookup from installed optional modules and
    cover qdx processing in the installed development-package test.
  * Find AOT fallback sources across the installed module search path.
  * Use LLVM's maintained Unicode conversion routines in linenoise instead of
    the legacy ConvertUTF sources rejected by Lintian.
  * Add reproducible snapshot source preparation, offline build and installed
    package qualification helpers, ELF/AOT checks, and artifact comparisons.
  * Verify detached debug files against runtime build IDs and debuglink CRCs.
  * Keep temporary build paths out of the installed CMake SDK configuration.
  * Qualify exact rebuilt artifacts when the same version exists in the PPA.
  * Version the pending changelog entry when preparing prerelease snapshots.
  * Include debug packages and removed package splits in lifecycle qualification.
  * Honor compiler file-prefix maps in QPP metadata and builtin source locations.
  * Make the installed compiler fingerprint independent of checkout paths.
  * Use source-relative documentation labels and omit Doxygen graph build caches.
  * Map final AOT artifact paths without changing input files or runtime resources.
  * Omit AOT build RPATHs at link time and keep build-tree discovery paths and
    temporary prefix-map options out of installed compiler binaries.
  * Restore the original HTTP streaming C++ entry point alongside the overload
    that reports connection reuse.
  * Correct date components when local time crosses the epoch in a negative zone.

 -- David Nichols <david@qore.org>  Fri, 06 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000
